# Programs whose card used to be built by a tools/playtests/*.keys script and
# a caption in gen_screens.py, now ordinary stanzas -- each with its own try
# line and a caption written for a stranger.  Screen toys and full-screen
# programs; every one ends with Ctrl-E from the harness whatever it is doing.
# backgammon and teachgammon draw their boards in one burst and are captured
# through an unthrottled path elsewhere; they are not here.

shot    worms
cap     Worms crawl about the screen at random, each leaving a trail, until
cap     you stop them.  A screen toy.  Control-C ends it.
try     worms
run     worms
wait    4
snap
wait    4
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    rain
cap     Raindrops land on the screen and spread in rings.  A screen toy.
cap     Control-C ends it.
try     rain
run     rain
wait    5
snap
wait    3
snap
wait    3
snap
wait    3
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    sonnet
cap     Writes a sonnet: fourteen numbered lines of iambic pentameter, the
cap     words drawn at random from its own lists.  Escape ends it.
try     sonnet
run     sonnet
wait    4
snap
wait    3
snap
send    \e
wait    2

shot    sc
cap     A spreadsheet.  Cells are named by column letter and row number; a
cap     leading `=' enters a number or formula in the current cell, the
cap     arrow keys or hjkl move, `?' lists the commands and `q' quits.
cap     Here 42 has been entered in cell A0.
try     sc
run     export TERM=vt100
wait    1
run     clear
wait    1
run     sc
wait    4
keys    =42
send    \r
wait    2
snap
send    q
wait    1
send    y
wait    2

shot    banner
cap     Prints its argument as tall letters made of `@', for a banner or a
cap     sign.
try     banner OS-9
run     banner OS-9
wait    5

shot    beav
cap     A binary editor and viewer, here on a file of the disk's own
cap     documentation: the offset, sixteen bytes in hexadecimal, and the
cap     same sixteen as characters.  Control-C leaves it.
run     builtin cd /dd/DOC
wait    1
run     clear
wait    1
try     beav README-CIO
run     beav README-CIO
wait    5
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    card
size    24 80
cap     A Towers of Hanoi solving itself, whose twelve disks are the lines
cap     of a season's greeting; the message assembles as the disks arrive on
cap     the far peg.
try     card
run     card
wait    16
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    nobs
cap     Cribbage against the computer.  It deals six cards, asks which two
cap     to lay away to the crib, then plays the hand and pegs the score on
cap     the board above.  Control-C leaves it.
try     nobs
run     nobs
wait    5
snap
wait    4
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    suicide
cap     An animation: a stick figure walks to the edge of a rooftop and
cap     jumps, with a long cry across the top of the screen.
try     suicide
run     suicide
wait    5
snap
wait    4
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    bite
cap     A skull draws itself, then bites; a screen toy.  `q' quits.
try     bite
run     bite
wait    4
snap
wait    3
snap
send    q
wait    2

shot    life
cap     Conway's Game of Life on a pattern from GAMES/LIFE -- here the
cap     glider, which walks across the board.  It detects a repeating
cap     pattern's period and prints it.  Control-C ends it.
try     life glider
run     builtin cd /dd/GAMES/LIFE
wait    1
run     clear
wait    1
run     life glider
wait    8
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    tess
size    30 80
cap     Beyond the Tesseract, a text adventure whose puzzles draw on physics
cap     and mathematics.  Two-word commands -- look, get all, use stack, n,
cap     s -- and about two hundred words are understood.  `-f' skips the
cap     title and scenario.
try     tess -f
run     tess -f
wait    5
send    look\r
wait    3
send    i\r
wait    3
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    world
size    30 80
cap     A text adventure set on an alien world where your landing party is
cap     stranded.  The usual verbs -- look, take, n, s -- move you and act;
cap     `quit' leaves.  It reads its text from GAMES/world.
try     world
run     world
wait    5
send    look\r
wait    4
snap
send    quit\r
wait    2
send    y\r
wait    2

shot    wish
cap     A one-line joke: it tells you what you wished for in hack, and what
cap     became of the game.
try     wish
run     wish
wait    4

shot    cam
cap     Camshaft design.  It asks the rocker ratio, then the valve lift at
cap     each crank angle of an intake lobe, and draws the lift curve.  The
cap     curve is drawn in Tektronix vectors, so on a character terminal the
cap     dialogue is the readable part.
try     cam
run     cam
wait    5
send    1.5\r
wait    2
send    0.4\r
wait    2
send    0.9\r
wait    2
send    1.4\r
wait    2
send    1.8\r
wait    2
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    lissaj
cap     Draws Lissajous figures -- the curve two oscillators trace against
cap     each other -- from the frequencies, duration and phase you give it.
cap     The curve is drawn in Tektronix vectors; on a character terminal the
cap     dialogue is the readable part.
try     lissaj
run     lissaj
wait    4
send    3\r
wait    2
send    2\r
wait    2
send    0\r
wait    2
snap
send    1\r
wait    1
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    piano
cap     Plays a scale through a tone generator: given a base note and a note
cap     length it sounds the notes.  It wants a third number as well; with
cap     no sound hardware to drive it answers `tuning - sorry' and stops.
try     piano 40 4 4
run     piano 40 4 4
wait    2
snap
